.TH SDL_REVISION 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_REVISION \- This macro is a string describing the source at a particular point in development.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_revision.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_REVISION \(dqSome arbitrary string decided at SDL build time\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This string is often generated from revision control\(aqs state at build time\[char46]
.PP
This string can be quite complex and does not follow any standard\[char46] For example, it might be something like \(dqSDL-prerelease-3\[char46]1\[char46]1-47-gf687e0732\(dq\[char46] It might also be user-defined at build time, so it\(aqs best to treat it as a clue in debugging forensics and not something the app will parse in any way\[char46]
.PP

.BR SDL_revision \[char46]h
must be included in your program explicitly if you want access to the
.BR SDL_REVISION
constant\[char46]

